# Cohort tarballs ARE committed release artifacts since the dsh
# 0.1.6-alpha.2 adoption: the kit's tarball install mode ships prebuilt
# dists (no bun/git-prepare wall), so `pnpm pack` outputs must be
# regenerated and committed on every cohort release (W-085/W-088).
# (No ignore rules left: the last stale-name entry —
# dsh-berget-usage-0.2.1.tgz from an intermediate 2026 repack — became the
# LIVE shipping name in the 0.2.2-rc.1 corridor and was un-ignored.
# Lesson: when rebake lands on a historically-ignored name, scrub the rule,
# else `git add -A` silently drops the tarball and only CI sees it. PR #70.)
